{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794306831,"nonce":"QLr92UOJFBTH/9fogK4lHMDyYZs=","title":"Paginate the per-user lists: GET /api/me/words and /api/me/clozes","message":"Neither has a LIMIT: words (cards.words, the word table in the user's Durable Object) returns every status the user has set, and clozes (api/src/worker/user.ts clozes(), ?documentId=) every cloze card from a text. Page them the way f0f6df0 plans for /api/documents: keyset, ?after=…\u0026limit=… with a default and a maximum, a next cursor in the response. The reader needs the whole set in both cases (word statuses for the sheet and highlighting, cloze starts for the open text), so loadWords and loadClozes follow pages until there's no next.\n\nGET /api/tags is unpaged too, but its rows come from the tag table (migration 0008), which only a migration adds to.","files":null}]}